INSERT INTO lr_explanation_steps (explanation_id, position, label, body) SELECT e.id, v.position, v.label, v.body FROM lr_explanations e JOIN lr_questions q ON q.id=e.question_id CROSS JOIN (VALUES (0, $pilot$Conclusion (clearly)$pilot$, $pilot$If you buy a Sturdimade, you can rely on being able to drive it for a very long distance.
  *rephrase:* Any Sturdimade you buy will go the distance.$pilot$), (1, $pilot$Evidence$pilot$, $pilot$Hundreds of longtime owners belong to Sturdimade's "long distance" club, and you can only join if your Sturdimade has hit 100,000 miles. Some members are at 300,000.$pilot$), (2, $pilot$Evaluate$pilot$, $pilot$*Given that ...* hundreds of Sturdimades have made it past 100,000 miles,
  *How could we argue that ...* you still can't rely on the Sturdimade *you* buy going the distance?

Look at the entry requirement for this club. The only way in is to already own a car that went 100,000 miles. So every car in the sample was picked *because* it lasted.

What about the Sturdimades that died at 30,000 miles? They're not in the club. They can't be. The club is designed to keep them out.

It's like proving that everyone who starts a marathon finishes it by surveying the people standing at the finish line.

And "hundreds" out of how many? If Sturdimade has sold ten million cars, a few hundred survivors tells us very little about the odds for yours.

Whenever an argument relies on a sample, we ask whether it's Too Small, Unrepresentative / Biased, or Self-Selecting. This one is biased by design.$pilot$), (3, $pilot$Goal$pilot$, $pilot$Let's look for an answer describing the Famous Sampling flaw: the author generalizes to all Sturdimades from a group that was chosen precisely because it already has the trait the conclusion wants to prove. A conversational version would sound like "fails to consider how many Sturdimades didn't last long enough to join the club."$pilot$)) v(position,label,body) WHERE q.qid=$pilot$PT109-S4-Q1$pilot$ AND e.style='single' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lr_explanation_steps s WHERE s.explanation_id=e.id) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
